3. [38;5;10mf9[0m — five of eight products in [38;5;10minvDenom[0m/[38;5;10mu[0m/[38;5;10mv[0m had swapped operands.[0m[0m
4. [38;5;10mf11[0m — four [38;5;10mx + m[0m/[38;5;10mc + m[0m stores in the later hue sectors had swapped operands; the existing comments claiming "GCC swaps" were wrong.[0m[0m
5. The [38;5;10maddss[0m/[38;5;10msubss[0m/[38;5;10mmulss[0m/[38;5;10mdivss[0m helpers used [38;5;10mif a.is_nan() {…}[0m branching. Correct in debug, but [1mLLVM restructures it at [38;5;10m-O[0m[22m: [38;5;10mf9[0m returned [38;5;10m0xffc00000[0m where C gives [38;5;10m0xffc58ed7[0m, passing in debug and failing in release. Rewritten as inline [38;5;10masm![0m.[0m[0m
